-# One day per page. A digest is a page-sized report, not a row — stacked among
-# the one-line activity rows it buried them and read badly itself — so it gets
-# a page, and the paginator walks back a day at a time.
.p-3
  %p.text-muted.small.mb-0
    Each day, summed up: what was asked, what ran, what is still stuck, and every work published to a community showcase. A day with nothing in it gets no digest. This is what the emailed summary will carry.

- if @notices.any?
  - @notices.each do |notice|
    = render 'admin/ledger/digest_day', notice: notice
  = paginate @notices
- else
  .admin-registry__empty
    %i.fa-solid.fa-book.admin-registry__empty-icon{'aria-hidden' => 'true'}
    %p.mb-1.fw-semibold.text-body No digests yet
    %p.mb-0.small.text-muted
      A digest is written each morning for the day before, whenever there was something to report.
